WEBVTT

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:13.190
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:13.190
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.830
<i>Overlooking the rows of houses and stores</i>

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:22.240
<i>from the highest vantage,</i>

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:27.350
<i>Such things as tears and sadness</i>

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:31.490
<i>will quickly vanish</i>

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:37.050
<i>The birds, wind, and sunshine...</i>

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:41.240
<i>...all are your friends</i>

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:46.310
<i>I'll carry this dream farther than far</i>

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:51.400
<i>...no matter the distance...</i>

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:58.160
<i>I long to fly freely</i>

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:02.440
<i>through the blue sky in my heart...</i>

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.370
<i>The far distant blue sky</i>

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:12.820
<i>It flows into tomorrow</i>

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:25.250
Takara Fansubs

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:35.560
<i>Romeo became friends with the angelic girl called Angeletta.</i>

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.600
<i>And then...</i>

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:42.860
<i>Angeletta, who had not left her room in ages due to her illness,</i>

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:49.470
<i>...received from Romeo the gift of the prodigious, azure sky of Milan.</i>

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:54.490
Episode 11:

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:54.490
An Angel's Abode

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:09.430
What a beautiful sight!

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.630
Aaah! It's the Wolf Pack!

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:16.030
"Wolf Pack"?

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:20.230
Damned kid!

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.530
Ah...! It's that...!

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:26.980
Stop!

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:54.090
Too bad!
I'm afraid this here's a dead-end.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:59.870
Heh heh... Looks like we've caught us a rat in a trap.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:09.430
What're you trying to pull...?!

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:14.030
The only rats caught in a trap here are YOU guys!

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:15.530
Who's that?!

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.580
I didn't think that it'd be this easy to catch you guys.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:29.230
My name's Rinaldo... but my friends all call me "Red".

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:30.530
Damn you!

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:35.250
I'm Tachioni -- also called "The Bull".

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:36.730
Dammit!

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.030
I'm Leo "The Louse"!

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:43.010
...and this guy is Faustino.

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:46.030
And I'm Nikita!

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:48.930
And together we form...
THE WOLF PACK!

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.130
Get 'em!

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:14.930
Did it! I got him!

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:20.530
Why don't you run along home before YOU get hurt too.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:22.730
Don't screw with me!

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:25.930
Leo!

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:26.930
Don't move!

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:30.130
One move and I'll slice this guy's face in two!

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:37.530
S... stop it, man!

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:40.630
I don't want a scar on my face!

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:46.030
Leo...

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:48.130
You keep still too.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.730
He's come! It's him!

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:06.330
Giovanni!

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:07.930
Giovanni?

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:18.530
That'll be enough, you guys.
I'll take it from here.

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:22.230
I told you not to move!

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.630
I'm serious, man!

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:28.630
Do it.

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:31.330
...if you got the guts to.

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:33.430
Just watch!

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:35.230
Don't!!

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:38.130
What's wrong?

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:39.830
GONNA DO IT OR NOT?!

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:07.630
We surrender!

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:10.630
Heeeelp...!

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.130
We did it!

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:13.910
What a victory for the Wolf Pack!

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:17.180
Man, there really ain't another one like you, Giovanni.

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:19.030
Fellow Wolves!

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:20.930
Fellow Wolves!

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:23.230
Hooray for the Wolf Pack!

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:44.230
Anzelmo!

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:46.630
Some timing YOU'VE got!

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:53.030
I just came from doing in another one of 'em!

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:55.230
I thought I was gonna die!

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:01.530
I stole this!

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:03.040
May I present our victory flag!

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:05.030
Victory flag, huh?

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:07.560
Pretty impressive for you, Anzelmo.

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:10.630
Why, this is simply MARVELOUS, Mr. Giovanni!

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:15.130
All right, let's go!

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:27.530
Why, that Anzelmo...

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:44.930
For your distinguished service today, I appoint you "general".

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:49.030
Yo! Rinaldo the Red!

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:50.530
General, huh?

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:51.890
What about me, Giovanni?

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:54.330
You'll appoint me general, too, won't you?

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:58.430
No way. You goofed big-time during last week's raid.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:02.330
Not only that, but there was that cop too!

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:04.930
Anzelmo was dead-on warning us about him coming!

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:07.430
That's right. That was a real feat.

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:09.430
Way to go, Anzelmo!

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:12.330
But I'M the one who knocked them down!

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:17.620
I'd say someone never puts their COGITATIVE muscles to any use...

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.430
What the hell's that supposed to mean!

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:21.630
Using those damned high-falootin' words on purpose!

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:26.510
Sounds like Anzelmo's saying that he's stronger than you up here...

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:29.230
S--say WHAT?! I'll beat the...!!

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:30.330
Stop it!

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:31.930
That's enough, Tachioni!

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:35.430
I can't just let him make a fool of me in front of everyone!

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:38.930
Can't you see it's this temper of yours that screws things up?!

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:42.430
True enough, you're pretty smart.

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:44.030
I'll give you that much.

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:45.530
Way to go, Mr. Royalty!

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:48.400
Hey, why don't you show "it" to us again. It's been a long time.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:50.030
Cool idea!

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:51.430
That doesn't sound half-bad!

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:53.230
I been waiting for this!

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:04.830
My mother and I were originally Russian royalty.

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:08.630
But I was kidnapped at the age of four by a group of bandits.

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:13.230
They attacked us suddenly in the middle of a snowstorm.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:16.330
And THIS is the scar that I received on that day.

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:28.830
It looks more and more like one each time I see it!

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:30.270
A scorpion-shaped scar.

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:35.330
Anzelmo!

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:38.130
You're special.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:40.630
Bring us some kind of treasure tomorrow morning.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:43.430
And if everybody agrees that it's cool enough a treasure...

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:44.630
...I'll make you a knight.

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:46.130
Giovanni!

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:47.830
Eh?

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:49.630
That's awesome, Anzelmo!

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:02.230
I was watching the whole battle...

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:06.130
And that Anzelmo is the lowest. He's a coward!

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:13.130
Oh, sorry! I forgot that he's your brother.

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:16.130
No, it's just as you say.

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:19.730
He has a lot of problems.

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:23.730
But there were so many good things about him when he was younger.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:27.130
Good things? About Anzelmo? No way.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:31.730
There are, still. I know it.

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:33.930
Being considerate is just hard for him.

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:38.630
Treasure, treasure, treasure!

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:42.530
Something that everybody'll find interesting?!

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:47.830
Shit! Giovanni, you damn jerk, you knew how hard that order would be!

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:51.630
Very well, Angeletta.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:55.330
I'll do as best as I can and try to find these GOOD points of his.

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:57.570
Will you really? Please do!

00:10:58.130 --> 00:10:59.330
Leave it to me!

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:07.430
What's wrong, Palmo?

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:11.330
I've got a favor to ask of you.

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:12.230
Yes?

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:16.630
Well... I was wondering if you could teach me how to read...?

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:17.380
To read?

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:20.130
I thought... It'd be neat if I could read lots of different things...

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:22.130
Like you and Alfredo do.

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:23.430
That's wonderful!

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:27.930
How about this? We could exchange letters.

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:29.630
Letters?

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:33.530
We write down our feelings, and what happened during our day.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:38.230
Write! Write! Write your love-letters!

00:12:10.030 --> 00:12:13.030
My, what an elegant-looking boy!

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:16.330
Why, I'll be painted if you don't look like a veritable PRINCE! No?

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:20.130
Well, now! You think so, too, do you, Palmo?

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:23.330
Now, what were those vagrants called...?

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:25.430
The "Wolf Pack", was it?

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:32.230
You and that bunch are like chalk and cheese -- like silk and sandpaper!

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:41.930
Why, I heard they raised a devil's rumpus again in town just yesterday.

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:49.930
Anzelmo, keep your hands clean of that filthy bunch, okay?

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:52.830
You're my precious treasure!

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:57.630
Of course, mom! I don't even want to get NEAR those guys!

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:02.930
Come now -- we're going out to buy your new shoes.

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:08.930
I'm appalled.

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:11.330
How you can say a black lie with a straight face like that?

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:14.030
You feel contempt for me, don't you.

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:17.630
I'm just timid...

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:21.730
When I'm with my Mom or my friends I always play up to them like that.

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:25.230
You know how it is, when you want people to like you?

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:28.430
You're talking, and -- you just wind up telling a lie.

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:31.230
Sure, I understand, but...

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:34.530
Please don't say anything to Mom about the Wolf Pack and me!

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:38.630
In exchange, I won't say anything about your secret, either.

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:41.230
Huh...?! Se...secret?

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:46.830
Angeletta has always been lonely...

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:49.830
I know she's happy to have you as a friend.

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:54.430
Please be a good friend to her.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:14:00.530
I won't tell anyone! This is a secret between just us three.

00:14:03.930 --> 00:14:06.930
I guess you probably don't trust me.

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:09.930
No no -- it makes me really happy!

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:14.630
Thank you, Anzelmo!

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:17.230
I won't say a thing about it -- about the Wolf Pack.

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:20.380
I promise!

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:41.580
Come in.

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:45.580
Angeletta!

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:46.580
Romeo!

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:50.480
It's just like you said!

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:52.780
Anzelmo really DOES have a good side!

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:54.080
This has really made me re-think him.

00:14:55.180 --> 00:14:57.580
He said he'd keep it a secret about us.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:59.580
Oh -- he knew all about it!

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:02.280
That guy! It turns out he's just a little fainthearted...

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:04.080
Despite what he does, his intentions are actually good.

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:07.180
From now on it's a secret between the THREE of us!

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:10.080
Really?

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:11.280
Yeah.

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:18.780
Oh -- here. I've a letter for you.

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:20.280
A letter?

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:22.980
Romeo! Where are you? Let's go!

00:15:22.990 --> 00:15:25.680
Oh crap! The boss is going to catch me!

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:27.280
Romeo! Here.

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:28.580
Romeo!

00:15:32.380 --> 00:15:33.580
Thank you!

00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:40.230
Oh, no!

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:49.300
<i>Angeletta began to panic.</i>

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:53.900
<i>The paper she'd given Romeo had been a page of her DIARY.</i>

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:07.980
Huh?

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:09.980
That's odd...

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:13.060
She said she would only write one line while we were just beginning...

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:16.180
I wonder what it says...

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:19.580
That's the "treasure"?

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:20.780
It's a love-letter!

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:21.880
A love letter?

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:26.780
I give up... I can't make out a thing!

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:34.680
Hey! If it isn't Romeo!

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:37.680
Anzelmo!

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:43.980
Is that one of Angeletta's letters?

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:46.280
I'm really stuck. I can't read it.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:49.680
Gee, if I could only read, I would help you out, but...

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:52.680
I'll have Angeletta read it to me tonight.

00:16:57.880 --> 00:17:00.980
Time to head back, else the boss is going to yell at me.

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:06.480
Romeo!

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:09.980
Oh no! Come quick!

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:13.980
I turned my head just for ONE second, and a thief...!

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:20.680
Stop!

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:24.480
Stop!

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:28.280
I'll cut him off over here!

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:32.210
Thanks, Anzelmo!

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:45.480
Suck on that, nitwit!

00:17:57.080 --> 00:18:00.080
I wish I could have seen this "Romeo's" face at that instant.

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:04.080
Jeez, you really ARE smart, Anzelmo!

00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:06.880
There ain't another one like him!

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:15.140
How's about you quit snickering, and cough up this letter of yours!

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:18.280
I wonder if everybody will accept it as okay...

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:19.880
'Course we will!

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:23.380
It's the biggest haul we've made since the Wolf Pack got together.

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:27.080
A love-letter, huh?

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:37.380
Read it.

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:00.580
"I am oppressed with sorrow..."

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:05.240
"...the merest thought of him is like an icy hand crushing my heart."

00:19:12.780 --> 00:19:18.350
"One shouldn't lie -- and yet Anzelmo has a habit of doing so."

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:22.780
Keep reading, Nikita.

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:26.510
"The heap of lies he tells his friends builds daily..."

00:19:26.550 --> 00:19:28.970
"...for example, that he is of Russian royal blood..."

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:34.510
S--stop it!

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:37.640
Keep going, Nikita.

00:19:40.180 --> 00:19:44.580
"It seems he has been saying that he got the scar on his shoulder when he was assaulted by bandits..."

00:19:44.730 --> 00:19:48.090
"...though it's only a scar from when he burned himself on the hearth two years ago."

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:52.150
"And every day sees a redoubling of his disparaging comments

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:54.970
about everybody in the Wolf Pack."

00:19:55.650 --> 00:20:00.150
"Seeing such an Anzelmo makes me so miserable I..."

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:39.200
Th--this is some kind of...!

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:41.190
Do it.

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:07.710
Hey boss...

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:11.730
Anzelmo was really nice to me today!

00:21:12.380 --> 00:21:13.850
He was?

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:17.200
Some thief stole my letter, though... but...

00:21:18.050 --> 00:21:20.480
Anzelmo's really good at heart, isn't he.

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:36.540
It's all... Romeo's fault.

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:41.480
I'll get revenge.

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:44.680
I'll make sure he never sees Angeletta again.

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:46.480
Never!

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:57.880
<i>Me -- a thief?!</i>

00:21:58.280 --> 00:22:02.280
<i>You say your stolen money was found in my bag?!</i>

00:22:03.160 --> 00:22:04.580
<i>I didn't do anything!</i>

00:22:04.890 --> 00:22:07.890
<i>You believe me, don't you, Anzelmo?</i>

00:22:08.420 --> 00:22:12.150
See you then!

00:22:08.420 --> 00:22:12.150
<i>To Vanish into the Misty City</i>

00:22:08.420 --> 00:22:12.150
Next time:

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:17.360
<i>"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"</i>

00:22:26.030 --> 00:22:30.130
<i>Si Si Ciao, why do the good times</i>

00:22:30.230 --> 00:22:34.430
<i>seem to end so soon?</i>

00:22:34.630 --> 00:22:38.630
<i>Si Si Ciao, we're all friends</i>

00:22:38.830 --> 00:22:42.830
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>

00:22:43.440 --> 00:22:47.740
<i>Your laughing voice dances</i>

00:22:47.740 --> 00:22:51.640
<i>Once again in the sky</i>

00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:58.940
<i>Your pocket bursting with memories</i>

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:04.540
<i>Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now</i>

00:23:04.740 --> 00:23:08.740
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>
